{
  "requirement": "If the accepted result cannot be deserialized into `R`, awaiting the builder\nreturns `ValidationError::Agent`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligation.** If the accepted result cannot be deserialized into `R`, awaiting the builder returns `ValidationError::Agent`. The test needs two things: a result the harness accepts, and an assertion that decoding failure surfaces as `ValidationError::Agent`.\n\n**Why the first loop case reaches decoding.** The harness does not check the submitted result against the schema. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tools.rs#fn[submitted_value]` only checks the envelope, which must have exactly one key, `result`. `impl[GraphSession<'_, '_, D>/Conversation]/fn[submit]` then returns `Submission::Accepted`. So `{\"result\":\"wrong\"}` is accepted by the harness. It cannot be deserialized into `bool`, so the failure happens at the decoding step. In `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]`, that step is `serde_json::from_value(value).map_err(... ValidationError::Agent ...)`.\n\n**Mapping to the test.** `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[typed_submission_references_resolve_and_invalid_results_are_agent_errors]` is marked `{test}` for this requirement.\n- It first submits a valid `Answer` and asserts the decoded `Decision::Yes`. This is the positive control.\n- In its loop, the first case is `{\"result\":\"wrong\"}` with `ctx.ask::<bool>()`. It asserts `matches!(…, Err(ValidationError::Agent(_)))`. This is the exact obligation: an accepted but undecodable result produces the `Agent` variant.\n- The other loop cases (`{}`, `{\"other\":true}`, and an extra key) exercise the envelope rule, `agent-harness.submission.invalid`. They are not decoding cases, but they do no harm.\n\n**Violations the test would catch.** The assertion would fail if decoding failure returned a different error variant, panicked, or yielded a default value or `Ok`.\n\n**Remaining observations.**\n- Only one target type (`bool`) is used for a failing decode. The requirement does not distinguish types, so this is not a gap.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[invalid_typed_submission_is_an_agent_error]` adds a related check with `Answer`, but it is not required here.\n\nNo gaps found.",
